:mb-3","margin_bottom_mobile":"mb-3"}},"richtext_PLzKaY":{"type":"richtext","settings":{"stars":false,"text":"<p>A floating deck, also called a freestanding deck, is a standalone platform that rests on the ground without being attached to your home. Unlike traditional decks that require deep concrete footings and complex construction, our floating deck kits use a revolutionary modular design that snaps together like building blocks.<\/p><h3><\/h3><h3><strong>Perfect for Any Backyard<\/strong><\/h3><ul><li>Uneven terrain? Our adjustable deck blocks level it out<\/li><li>Mature trees? No digging means you won't damage roots<\/li><li>Renters? Take it with you when you move<\/li><li>Temporary solution? Easy to disassemble and relocate<\/li><\/ul><h3><\/h3><h3><strong>Faster Than Traditional Decks<\/strong><\/h3><p>Traditional deck building takes 2-3 weeks and costs $8,000-$15,000. Our floating deck kits install in few hours and cost 40% less.<\/p><h3><\/h3><h3><strong>Complete Creative Freedom<\/strong><\/h3><p>Place your floating deck anywhere in your yard – near the pool, in a sunny corner, under shade trees, or as a backyard retreat away from the house.<\/p>","richtext_class":"richtext-md list-content h3-margin-bottom","text_color":"","margin_bottom_desktop":"","margin_bottom_mobile":""}}},"block_order":["image_AhqxAV","richtext_QAiRGa","richtext_PLzKaY"],"settings":{"media_position":"right","media_position_mobile":"top","background_color":"#ffffff","section_id":"","vertical_padding_section":"48px | 48px","container_spacing":"px-container-md","responsive_visibility":""}},"compare_table_custom_TDtiH3":{"type":"compare-table-custom","name":"Comparison Section","settings":{"heading":"The Problem with Traditional Deck Building","left_content":"<h3><strong>Traditional Deck Building:<\/strong><\/h3><ul><li>$8,000 - $15,000 contractor fees <\/li><li>2-3 weeks of construction noise and mess<\/li><li>Scheduling delays and no-shows<\/li><li>Hidden fees and surprise costs<\/li><li>Digging deep holes and disturbing your yard<\/li><li>Complex permits and inspections<\/li><li>Specialized tools and skills required<\/li><\/ul><p><\/p>","right_content":"<h3><strong>A-DIY Floating Deck Kit:<\/strong><\/h3><ul><li>Save up to $5,000+ in labor costs<\/li><li>Install in few hours<\/li><li>No waiting on contractors<\/li><li>All-inclusive pricing<\/li><li>Simple deck blocks – no digging required<\/li><li>Often no permits needed<\/li><li>Just a power drill – we include the drill bit<\/li><\/ul>","bottom_content":"<p>We've taken the complexity, cost, and hassle out of building floating deck boards. Our<a href=\"https:\/\/a-diy.com\/\"> <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">DIY deck kits<\/span><\/a> arrive with every piece pre-cut, pre-drilled, and engineered to fit together perfectly. You don't need to be a contractor. You just need a free afternoon and a power drill.<\/p>","background_color":"#ece8e4"}},"step_section_JPUq4B":{"type":"step-section","name":"Three-Step Section","settings":{"heading":"3 Simple Steps to Your Dream Floating Deck","step1_content":"<h3><strong>Step 1: Choose Your Floating Deck Kit and Size<\/strong><\/h3><p>Select your size and material (pressure-treated or composite). Not sure which size? Our design team offers free consultations to help you find the perfect fit for your backyard.<\/p>","step2_content":"<h3><strong>Step 2: Unbox & Assemble<\/strong><\/h3><p>Your floating deck kit arrives with everything you need, including lumber, screws, deck blocks, a drill bit, and assembly instructions. Follow our step-by-step guide and watch your deck come together in few hours.<\/p>","step3_content":"<h3><strong>Step 3: Enjoy Your New Outdoor Space<\/strong><\/h3><p>That's it! In less time than it takes to watch a movie, you've created a beautiful outdoor space perfect for BBQs, relaxation, and making memories. Add furniture, plants, or a pergola, and your new floating deck is ready for anything.<\/p>","background_color":"#ffffff"}