shopify:\/\/shop_images\/transform-your-backyard-this-weekend-with-a-diy-floating-deck-kits.png"}},"richtext_8Gc3h8":{"type":"richtext","settings":{"stars":false,"text":"","richtext_class":"text-16\/14-500","text_color":"","margin_bottom_desktop":"md:mb-3","margin_bottom_mobile":"mb-2"}},"richtext_bbKDAQ":{"type":"richtext","settings":{"stars":false,"text":"<h2><strong>Transform Your Backyard This Weekend with A-DIY Floating Deck Kits<\/strong><\/h2>","richtext_class":"richtext-md","text_color":"","margin_bottom_desktop":"md:mb-3","margin_bottom_mobile":"mb-2"}},"richtext_gPnCVe":{"type":"richtext","settings":{"stars":false,"text":"<p>Skip the contractor and weeks of construction mess. A-DIY's professional-grade floating deck kits arrive ready to assemble with everything you need. Just unbox, connect, and enjoy your new outdoor living space the same day. Whether you're creating an entertainment hub for summer BBQs or a peaceful retreat in your garden, our modular deck kits make it simple to build the patio you've always wanted. Save thousands compared to hiring a contractor and feel the pride of building it yourself.<\/p>","richtext_class":"richtext-md","text_color":"","margin_bottom_desktop":"md:mb-12","margin_bottom_mobile":"mb-6"}},"buttons_jtrXy3":{"type":"buttons","settings":{"button_primary_text":"Shop Your Deck Kit","button_primary_url":"https:\/\/a-diy.com\/shop\/","button_primary_class":"button-primary","button_secondary_text":"","button_secondary_url":"","button_secondary_class":""}}},"block_order":["image_iK3MDJ","richtext_8Gc3h8","richtext_bbKDAQ","richtext_gPnCVe","buttons_jtrXy3"],"name":"Media With Text","settings":{"media_position":"right","media_position_mobile":"top","background_color":"#ffffff","section_id":"","vertical_padding_section":"32px\/24px | 48px","container_spacing":"px-container-md","responsive_visibility":""}},"preset_faq_CwTqgX":{"type":"preset__faq","blocks":{"richtext_zEPG48":{"type":"richtext","settings":{"title":"<h2><strong>FAQs<\/strong><\/h2>","page_content":"","use_page_content":false,"content_class":"richtext-md","margin_top_bottom_left_right":"0 | 40px\/32px | 0 | 0","max_w_flex_col_row_order_align":"100% | unset | 1 | 1 | unset | center","responsive_visibility":"","hide_if_empty":"none","responsive_breakpoint":"768px","anchor_id":"","color_override":""}},"collapsible_bwtd3k":{"type":"collapsible","settings":{"label":"<strong>Do I need a permit for a floating deck?<\/strong>","content":"<p>In most areas, ground-level floating decks under a certain height (typically 30\") don't require permits because they're not permanently attached to a structure. However, regulations vary by location. We recommend checking with your local building department. Even if a permit isn't required, our floating deck kits are engineered to exceed standard building codes.<\/p>","page_content":"","accordion_class":"accordion","default_state":"closed","margin_top_bottom_left_right":"0 | 24px | 0 | 0","max_w_flex_col_row_order_align":"905px | unset | 1 | 1 | unset | left","responsive_visibility":"","hide_if_empty":"none","responsive_breakpoint":"768px","anchor_id":""}},"collapsible_FhpDi8":{"type":"collapsible","settings":{"label":"<strong>How long does it take to assemble a floating deck kit?<\/strong>","content":"<p>Most customers complete assembly in under 1 hour. The exact time depends on the size of your deck and number of helpers, but our patent-pending design eliminates all cutting, measuring, and guesswork. Everything fits together perfectly, just like Lego blocks.<\/p>","page_content":"","accordion_class":"accordion","default_state":"closed","margin_top_bottom_left_right":"0 | 24px | 0 | 0","max_w_flex_col_row_order_align":"905px | unset | 1 | 1 | unset | left","responsive_visibility":"","hide_if_empty":"none","responsive_breakpoint":"768px","anchor_id":""}},"collapsible_Ji9w8f":{"type":"collapsible","settings":{"label":"<strong>What tools do I need?<\/strong>","content":"<p>All you need is a power drill. We even include the drill bit! No saws, no special tools, no trips to the hardware store.<\/p>","page_content":"","accordion_class":"accordion","default_state":"closed","margin_top_bottom_left_right":"0 | 24px | 0 | 0","max_w_flex_col_row_order_align":"905px | unset | 1 | 1 | unset | left","responsive_visibility":"","hide_if_empty":"none","responsive_breakpoint":"768px","anchor_id":""}},"collapsible_xRCEmR":{"type":"collapsible","settings":{"label":"<strong>Can I install a floating deck on uneven ground?<\/strong>","content":"<p>Absolutely! Our adjustable deck blocks allow you to create a perfectly level deck surface on uneven terrain. Simply adjust the height of each block to compensate for slopes or dips in your yard.<\/p>","page_content":"","accordion_class":"accordion","default_state":"closed","margin_top_bottom_left_right":"0 | 24px | 0 | 0","max_w_flex_col_row_order_align":"905px | unset | 1 | 1 | unset | left","responsive_visibility":"","hide_if_empty":"none","responsive_breakpoint":"768px","anchor_id":""}},"collapsible_HrYWCC":{"type":"collapsible","settings":{"label":"<strong>How much does a floating deck kit cost?<\/strong>","content":"<p>Our floating deck kits range from $2,000-$4,000 depending on size and material choice (pressure-treated or composite). This is 40-60% less expensive than hiring a contractor, who typically charges $8,000-$15,000 for comparable work.<\/p>","page_content":"","accordion_class":"accordion","default_state":"closed","margin_top_bottom_left_right":"0 | 24px | 0 | 0","max_w_flex_col_row_order_align":"905px | unset | 1 | 1 | unset | left","responsive_visibility":"","hide_if_empty":"none","responsive_breakpoint":"768px","anchor_id":""}},"collapsible_JzMhTQ":{"type":"collapsible","settings":{"label":"<strong>Can I move or relocate my floating deck?<\/strong>","content":"<p>Yes! One of the biggest advantages of floating decks is that they're not permanent. You can disassemble and relocate your A-DIY floating deck kit if you move or redesign your yard.<\/p>","page_content":"","accordion_class":"accordion","default_state":"closed","margin_top_bottom_left_right":"0 | 24px | 0 | 0","max_w_flex_col_row_order_align":"905px | unset | 1 | 1 | unset | left","responsive_visibility":"","hide_if_empty":"none","responsive_breakpoint":"768px","anchor_id":""}},"collapsible_eGzRUC":{"type":"collapsible","settings":{"label":"<strong>What's included in the floating deck kit?<\/strong>","content":"<p>Everything! All lumber pieces (pre-cut and pre-drilled), all galvanized screws, deck blocks (TuffBlocks), drill bit, and access to our 3D assembly app. The only thing you need to supply is a power drill.<\/p>","page_content":"","accordion_class":"accordion","default_state":"closed","margin_top_bottom_left_right":"0 | 24px | 0 | 0","max_w_flex_col_row_order_align":"905px | unset | 1 | 1 | unset | left","responsive_visibility":"","hide_if_empty":"none","responsive_breakpoint":"768px","anchor_id":""}},"collapsible_7CJVLp":{"type":"collapsible","settings":{"label":"<strong>How do I know what size floating deck kit to order?<\/strong>","content":"<p>We offer several standard sizes to fit most backyards. If you're unsure, our design team provides free consultations. Send us photos and measurements of your space, and we'll recommend the perfect size.<\/p>","page_content":"","accordion_class":"accordion","default_state":"closed","margin_top_bottom_left_right":"0 | 24px | 0 | 0","max_w_flex_col_row_order_align":"905px | unset | 1 | 1 | unset | left","responsive_visibility":"","hide_if_empty":"none","responsive_breakpoint":"768px","anchor_id":""}},"collapsible_kTmVCR":{"type":"collapsible","settings":{"label":"<strong>What's the difference between pressure-treated and composite floating deck kits?<\/strong>","content":"<p>Pressure-treated kits use premium Grade 1 KDAT lumber, natural wood that's affordable and can be stained. Composite kits use low-maintenance synthetic decking that never needs sealing and comes with a 25-y